{"documents": [{"id": "scierc:train:0", "source": "scierc", "text": "English is shown to be trans-context-free on the basis of coordinations of the respectively type that involve strictly syntactic cross-serial agreement .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 153, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "English", "type": "Material", "start": 0, "end": 1}, {"text": "coordinations", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 10, "end": 11}, {"text": "strictly syntactic cross-serial agreement", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 17, "end": 21}], "orig_id": "55b1c509-5b1a-49b0-a090-19f64bc8bb55"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:1", "source": "scierc", "text": "The agreement in question involves number in nouns and reflexive pronouns and is syntactic rather than semantic in nature because grammatical number in English , like grammatical gender in languages such as French , is partly arbitrary .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 237, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "agreement", "type": "Generic", "start": 1, "end": 2}, {"text": "nouns", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 7, "end": 8}, {"text": "reflexive pronouns", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 9, "end": 11}, {"text": "grammatical number", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 20, "end": 22}, {"text": "English", "type": "Material", "start": 23, "end": 24}, {"text": "grammatical gender", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 26, "end": 28}, {"text": "languages", "type": "Material", "start": 29, "end": 30}, {"text": "French", "type": "Material", "start": 32, "end": 33}], "orig_id": "9da0f0cd-1618-443a-b10f-bfaa2f4cf268"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:2", "source": "scierc", "text": "The formal proof , which makes crucial use of the Interchange Lemma of Ogden et al. , is so constructed as to be valid even if English is presumed to contain grammatical sentences in which respectively operates across a pair of coordinate phrases one of whose members has fewer conjuncts than the other ; it thus goes through whatever the facts may be regarding constructions with unequal numbers of conjuncts in the scope of respectively , whereas other arguments have foundered on this problem .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 497, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "Interchange Lemma", "type": "Method", "start": 10, "end": 12}, {"text": "English", "type": "Material", "start": 26, "end": 27}], "orig_id": "bb668fe7-7c3e-4d6d-8cab-1fd1fa2f6cbc"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:3", "source": "scierc", "text": "In this paper , a novel method to learn the intrinsic object structure for robust visual tracking is proposed .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 111, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "method", "type": "Method", "start": 6, "end": 7}, {"text": "intrinsic object structure", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 10, "end": 13}, {"text": "robust visual tracking", "type": "Task", "start": 14, "end": 17}], "orig_id": "5921ecea-02e8-4041-88e1-6a9497a2dd2f"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:4", "source": "scierc", "text": "The basic assumption is that the parameterized object state lies on a low dimensional manifold and can be learned from training data .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 134, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "parameterized object state", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 6, "end": 9}, {"text": "low dimensional manifold", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 12, "end": 15}], "orig_id": "44c7fa11-bad5-45ed-9a58-2bea29a2269c"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:5", "source": "scierc", "text": "Based on this assumption , firstly we derived the dimensionality reduction and density estimation algorithm for unsupervised learning of object intrinsic representation , the obtained non-rigid part of object state reduces even to 2 dimensions .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 245, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "dimensionality reduction and density estimation algorithm", "type": "Method", "start": 9, "end": 15}, {"text": "unsupervised learning of object intrinsic representation", "type": "Task", "start": 16, "end": 22}, {"text": "object intrinsic representation", "type": "Method", "start": 19, "end": 22}, {"text": "non-rigid part of object state", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 25, "end": 30}], "orig_id": "aa279a30-3957-4b80-88de-8a1d87c39c2f"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:6", "source": "scierc", "text": "Secondly the dynamical model is derived and trained based on this intrinsic representation .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 92, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "dynamical model", "type": "Method", "start": 2, "end": 4}, {"text": "intrinsic representation", "type": "Method", "start": 11, "end": 13}], "orig_id": "73abc0b3-8ef3-45e7-954c-f0cae3650bde"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:7", "source": "scierc", "text": "Thirdly the learned intrinsic object structure is integrated into a particle-filter style tracker .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 99, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "intrinsic object structure", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 3, "end": 6}, {"text": "particle-filter style tracker", "type": "Method", "start": 10, "end": 13}], "orig_id": "5469d175-6d3e-44aa-818a-ddca0d9b950e"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:8", "source": "scierc", "text": "We will show that this intrinsic object representation has some interesting properties and based on which the newly derived dynamical model makes particle-filter style tracker more robust and reliable .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 202, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "intrinsic object representation", "type": "Method", "start": 5, "end": 8}, {"text": "dynamical model", "type": "Method", "start": 19, "end": 21}, {"text": "particle-filter style tracker", "type": "Method", "start": 22, "end": 25}], "orig_id": "72046a2f-d56f-4e87-971a-9de3e7180f5a"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:9", "source": "scierc", "text": "Experiments show that the learned tracker performs much better than existing trackers on the tracking of complex non-rigid motions such as fish twisting with self-occlusion and large inter-frame lip motion .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 207, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "tracker", "type": "Generic", "start": 5, "end": 6}, {"text": "trackers", "type": "Generic", "start": 11, "end": 12}, {"text": "tracking of complex non-rigid motions", "type": "Task", "start": 14, "end": 19}, {"text": "complex non-rigid motions", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 16, "end": 19}, {"text": "fish twisting", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 21, "end": 23}, {"text": "self-occlusion", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 24, "end": 25}, {"text": "inter-frame lip motion", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 27, "end": 30}], "orig_id": "72c51793-3031-41c8-ba0c-1a3f1200152c"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:10", "source": "scierc", "text": "The proposed method also has the potential to solve other type of tracking problems .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 85, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "method", "type": "Generic", "start": 2, "end": 3}, {"text": "tracking problems", "type": "Task", "start": 12, "end": 14}], "orig_id": "8549a757-e128-4e28-bc3d-53202df6ba9d"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:11", "source": "scierc", "text": "In this paper , we present a digital signal processor ( DSP ) implementation of real-time statistical voice conversion ( VC ) for silent speech enhancement and electrolaryngeal speech enhancement .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 197, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "digital signal processor ( DSP ) implementation", "type": "Method", "start": 7, "end": 14}, {"text": "real-time statistical voice conversion ( VC )", "type": "Method", "start": 15, "end": 22}, {"text": "silent speech enhancement", "type": "Task", "start": 23, "end": 26}, {"text": "electrolaryngeal speech enhancement", "type": "Task", "start": 27, "end": 30}], "orig_id": "1db83635-f2e0-417f-ba11-570e092727d1"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:12", "source": "scierc", "text": "As a silent speech interface , we focus on non-audible murmur ( NAM ) , which can be used in situations where audible speech is not acceptable .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 144, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "silent speech interface", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 2, "end": 5}, {"text": "non-audible murmur ( NAM )", "type": "Material", "start": 9, "end": 14}, {"text": "audible speech", "type": "Material", "start": 22, "end": 24}], "orig_id": "bba7885a-a6ea-41bf-981d-fc279e7e23ec"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:13", "source": "scierc", "text": "Electrolaryngeal speech is one of the typical types of alaryngeal speech produced by an alternative speaking method for laryngectomees .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 136, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "Electrolaryngeal speech", "type": "Material", "start": 0, "end": 2}, {"text": "alaryngeal speech", "type": "Material", "start": 9, "end": 11}, {"text": "speaking method", "type": "Method", "start": 15, "end": 17}, {"text": "laryngectomees", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 18, "end": 19}], "orig_id": "dee60f75-e8e7-4622-9aff-90d9fe1087a2"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:14", "source": "scierc", "text": "However , the sound quality of NAM and electrolaryngeal speech suffers from lack of naturalness .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 97, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "sound quality", "type": "Metric", "start": 3, "end": 5}, {"text": "NAM", "type": "Material", "start": 6, "end": 7}, {"text": "NAM and electrolaryngeal speech", "type": "Material", "start": 6, "end": 10}], "orig_id": "fffbab39-2289-4591-a9e0-905a0f8041ac"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:15", "source": "scierc", "text": "VC has proven to be one of the promising approaches to address this problem , and it has been successfully implemented on devices with sufficient computational resources .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 171, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "VC", "type": "Method", "start": 0, "end": 1}, {"text": "it", "type": "Generic", "start": 16, "end": 17}, {"text": "devices", "type": "Generic", "start": 22, "end": 23}, {"text": "sufficient computational resources", "type": "Material", "start": 24, "end": 27}], "orig_id": "38cc771d-6767-4b28-89dd-7e4b7b65b1e3"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:16", "source": "scierc", "text": "An implementation on devices that are highly portable but have limited computational resources would greatly contribute to its practical use .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 142, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "devices", "type": "Generic", "start": 3, "end": 4}, {"text": "limited computational resources", "type": "Material", "start": 10, "end": 13}], "orig_id": "180292cf-86df-47ee-8b95-9320912f1f48"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:17", "source": "scierc", "text": "In this paper we further implement real-time VC on a DSP .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 58, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "real-time VC", "type": "Method", "start": 6, "end": 8}, {"text": "DSP", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 10, "end": 11}], "orig_id": "1eaf55e6-8069-4235-a7ee-dc5667e43cfa"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:18", "source": "scierc", "text": "To implement the two speech enhancement systems based on real-time VC , one from NAM to a whispered voice and the other from electrolaryngeal speech to a natural voice , we propose several methods for reducing computational cost while preserving conversion accuracy .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 267, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "speech enhancement systems", "type": "Method", "start": 4, "end": 7}, {"text": "real-time VC", "type": "Method", "start": 9, "end": 11}, {"text": "one", "type": "Generic", "start": 12, "end": 13}, {"text": "NAM", "type": "Material", "start": 14, "end": 15}, {"text": "whispered voice", "type": "Material", "start": 17, "end": 19}, {"text": "other", "type": "Generic", "start": 21, "end": 22}, {"text": "electrolaryngeal speech", "type": "Material", "start": 23, "end": 25}, {"text": "natural voice", "type": "Material", "start": 27, "end": 29}, {"text": "methods", "type": "Generic", "start": 33, "end": 34}, {"text": "computational cost", "type": "Metric", "start": 36, "end": 38}, {"text": "conversion accuracy", "type": "Metric", "start": 40, "end": 42}], "orig_id": "980d96e8-aba5-41fc-8b10-ab2bdef408ea"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:19", "source": "scierc", "text": "We conduct experimental evaluations and show that real-time VC is capable of running on a DSP with little degradation .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 119, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "real-time VC", "type": "Method", "start": 7, "end": 9}, {"text": "DSP", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 15, "end": 16}], "orig_id": "29895e4a-dc41-4732-973d-2416ade1e4d4"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:20", "source": "scierc", "text": "We propose a method that automatically generates paraphrase sets from seed sentences to be used as reference sets in objective machine translation evaluation measures like BLEU and NIST .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 187, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "method", "type": "Generic", "start": 3, "end": 4}, {"text": "paraphrase", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 7, "end": 8}, {"text": "machine translation evaluation measures", "type": "Metric", "start": 20, "end": 24}, {"text": "BLEU", "type": "Metric", "start": 25, "end": 26}, {"text": "NIST", "type": "Metric", "start": 27, "end": 28}], "orig_id": "44899a82-1dda-46c4-9f0f-01e816aca59d"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:21", "source": "scierc", "text": "We measured the quality of the paraphrases produced in an experiment , i.e. , ( i ) their grammaticality : at least 99 % correct sentences ; ( ii ) their equivalence in meaning : at least 96 % correct paraphrases either by meaning equivalence or entailment ; and , ( iii ) the amount of internal lexical and syntactical variation in a set of paraphrases : slightly superior to that of hand-produced sets .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 405, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "paraphrases", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 6, "end": 7}, {"text": "grammaticality", "type": "Metric", "start": 18, "end": 19}, {"text": "equivalence in meaning", "type": "Metric", "start": 31, "end": 34}, {"text": "paraphrases", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 40, "end": 41}, {"text": "meaning equivalence", "type": "Method", "start": 43, "end": 45}, {"text": "entailment", "type": "Method", "start": 46, "end": 47}, {"text": "internal lexical and syntactical variation", "type": "Metric", "start": 56, "end": 61}, {"text": "paraphrases", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 65, "end": 66}, {"text": "hand-produced sets", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 72, "end": 74}], "orig_id": "c7a747b1-c03d-4ea6-b521-aab826512709"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:22", "source": "scierc", "text": "The paraphrase sets produced by this method thus seem adequate as reference sets to be used for MT evaluation .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 111, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "paraphrase", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 1, "end": 2}, {"text": "method", "type": "Generic", "start": 6, "end": 7}, {"text": "MT evaluation", "type": "Task", "start": 17, "end": 19}], "orig_id": "2dd432e8-3432-4386-b91a-dd476eaa08ca"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:23", "source": "scierc", "text": "Graph unification remains the most expensive part of unification-based grammar parsing .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 88, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "Graph unification", "type": "Task", "start": 0, "end": 2}, {"text": "unification-based grammar parsing", "type": "Task", "start": 8, "end": 11}], "orig_id": "26a03dfc-f2e8-4ddb-933a-8ebb8f11a54a"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:24", "source": "scierc", "text": "We focus on one speed-up element in the design of unification algorithms : avoidance of copying of unmodified subgraphs .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 121, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "speed-up element", "type": "Method", "start": 4, "end": 6}, {"text": "unification algorithms", "type": "Method", "start": 10, "end": 12}, {"text": "copying of unmodified subgraphs", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 15, "end": 19}, {"text": "unmodified subgraphs", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 17, "end": 19}], "orig_id": "285e537d-70d6-431d-8dfa-261dee01e86c"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:25", "source": "scierc", "text": "We propose a method of attaining such a design through a method of structure-sharing which avoids log ( d ) overheads often associated with structure-sharing of graphs without any use of costly dependency pointers .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 215, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "method", "type": "Generic", "start": 3, "end": 4}, {"text": "structure-sharing", "type": "Method", "start": 13, "end": 14}, {"text": "log ( d ) overheads", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 16, "end": 21}, {"text": "structure-sharing of graphs", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 24, "end": 27}, {"text": "dependency pointers", "type": "Method", "start": 32, "end": 34}], "orig_id": "ebefbfbe-f72d-4f42-8e31-9adb0e703e95"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:26", "source": "scierc", "text": "The proposed scheme eliminates redundant copying while maintaining the quasi-destructive scheme 's ability to avoid over copying and early copying combined with its ability to handle cyclic structures without algorithmic additions .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 232, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "scheme", "type": "Generic", "start": 2, "end": 3}, {"text": "redundant copying", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 4, "end": 6}, {"text": "quasi-destructive scheme 's ability", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 9, "end": 13}, {"text": "over copying", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 15, "end": 17}, {"text": "early copying", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 18, "end": 20}, {"text": "cyclic structures", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 26, "end": 28}], "orig_id": "bfa59af2-2dad-4617-aa1c-092351ca9d72"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:27", "source": "scierc", "text": "We describe a novel technique and implemented system for constructing a subcategorization dictionary from textual corpora .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 123, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "system", "type": "Generic", "start": 7, "end": 8}, {"text": "subcategorization dictionary", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 11, "end": 13}, {"text": "textual corpora", "type": "Material", "start": 14, "end": 16}], "orig_id": "79e11232-51a7-459b-bcef-f7fb0644347e"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:28", "source": "scierc", "text": "Each dictionary entry encodes the relative frequency of occurrence of a comprehensive set of subcategorization classes for English .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 132, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "relative frequency of occurrence", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 5, "end": 9}], "orig_id": "dd1d6f0a-a378-4500-896d-63786b098c5a"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:29", "source": "scierc", "text": "An initial experiment , on a sample of 14 verbs which exhibit multiple complementation patterns , demonstrates that the technique achieves accuracy comparable to previous approaches , which are all limited to a highly restricted set of subcategorization classes .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 263, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [], "orig_id": "e6069a4f-0ae2-4e2b-afea-577872c8633c"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:30", "source": "scierc", "text": "We also demonstrate that a subcategorization dictionary built with the system improves the accuracy of a parser by an appreciable amount", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 136, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "subcategorization dictionary", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 5, "end": 7}, {"text": "system", "type": "Generic", "start": 10, "end": 11}, {"text": "accuracy", "type": "Metric", "start": 13, "end": 14}, {"text": "parser", "type": "Method", "start": 16, "end": 17}], "orig_id": "17d40b47-cdb1-4294-aaf1-e023fa40a4fd"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:31", "source": "scierc", "text": "The introduction of prior knowledge has greatly enhanced numerous purely low-level driven image processing algorithms .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 119, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "prior knowledge", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 3, "end": 5}, {"text": "low-level driven image processing algorithms", "type": "Method", "start": 10, "end": 15}], "orig_id": "72dba4c7-f012-4eeb-bded-a63863fecb84"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:32", "source": "scierc", "text": "In this work , we focus on the problem of non-rigid image registration .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 72, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "non-rigid image registration", "type": "Task", "start": 10, "end": 13}], "orig_id": "6c523692-11dc-4b31-85ad-1a854e8f7008"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:33", "source": "scierc", "text": "A number of powerful registration criteria have been developed in the last decade , most prominently the criterion of maximum mutual information .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 146, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "registration criteria", "type": "Metric", "start": 4, "end": 6}, {"text": "maximum mutual information", "type": "Metric", "start": 19, "end": 22}], "orig_id": "abe88420-31cb-49b7-8cc9-dfa0f2367edf"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:34", "source": "scierc", "text": "Although this criterion provides for good registration results in many applications , it remains a purely low-level criterion .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 127, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "criterion", "type": "Generic", "start": 2, "end": 3}, {"text": "it", "type": "Generic", "start": 12, "end": 13}, {"text": "low-level criterion", "type": "Metric", "start": 16, "end": 18}], "orig_id": "4b2aa2d8-56fe-4956-89a3-995a3c3b70b9"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:35", "source": "scierc", "text": "As a consequence , registration results will deteriorate once this low-level information is corrupted , due to noise , partial occlusions or missing image structure .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 166, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "registration", "type": "Task", "start": 4, "end": 5}, {"text": "low-level information", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 10, "end": 12}, {"text": "noise", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 17, "end": 18}, {"text": "partial occlusions", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 19, "end": 21}, {"text": "missing image structure", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 22, "end": 25}], "orig_id": "e1960fa6-54ed-4ba3-80cd-6c763c28610e"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:36", "source": "scierc", "text": "In this paper , we will develop a Bayesian framework that allows to impose statistically learned prior knowledge about the joint intensity distribution into image registration methods .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 185, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "Bayesian framework", "type": "Method", "start": 8, "end": 10}, {"text": "statistically learned prior knowledge", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 14, "end": 18}, {"text": "joint intensity distribution", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 20, "end": 23}, {"text": "image registration methods", "type": "Method", "start": 24, "end": 27}], "orig_id": "290a494e-7449-4c56-a1d1-a46a23b4f5cc"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:37", "source": "scierc", "text": "The prior is given by a kernel density estimate on the space of joint intensity distributions computed from a representative set of pre-registered image pairs .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 160, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "prior", "type": "Generic", "start": 1, "end": 2}, {"text": "kernel density estimate", "type": "Method", "start": 6, "end": 9}, {"text": "joint intensity distributions", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 13, "end": 16}, {"text": "pre-registered image pairs", "type": "Material", "start": 22, "end": 25}], "orig_id": "8f5454b8-940f-4e66-8024-990ead2d572a"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:38", "source": "scierc", "text": "This nonparametric prior accurately models previously learned intensity relations between various image modalities and slice locations .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 136, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "intensity relations", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 7, "end": 9}, {"text": "image modalities", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 11, "end": 13}, {"text": "slice locations", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 14, "end": 16}], "orig_id": "c19643fc-4b78-4b77-a708-151193695655"}}, {"id": "scierc:train:39", "source": "scierc", "text": "Experimental results demonstrate that the resulting registration process is more robust to missing low-level information as it favors intensity correspondences statistically consistent with the learned intensity distributions .", "segments": [{"ordinal": 0, "start": 0, "end": 227, "parent": null, "level": 0}], "uri": null, "observed_at": 0, "grants": ["public"], "metadata": {"split": "train", "entities": [{"text": "registration process", "type": "Method", "start": 6, "end": 8}, {"text": "missing low-level information", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 12, "end": 15}, {"text": "it", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 16, "end": 17}, {"text": "intensity correspondences", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 18, "end": 20}, {"text": "intensity distributions", "type": "OtherScientificTerm", "start": 25, "end": 27}], "orig_id": "201a7247-a87a-4f4f-8581-fb376a5335b7"}}], "triples": [{"subject": "nouns", "predicate": "Conjunction", "object": "reflexive pronouns", "question_id": null, "document_id": "scierc:train:1"}, {"subject": "grammatical gender", "predicate": "Feature-of", "object": "languages", "question_id": null, "document_id": "scierc:train